      "math_academy_id": "e-8491",
      "problem": "The discrete random variable $X\\in \\mathbb Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(X = -1)$ can be approximated as $P(a\\leq Y \\leq b).$ Find the values of $a$ and $b.$",
      "worked_solution": "We construct an interval around $X=-1$ with a radius of $0.5{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14129188/assets/e92a0fb229125f6a9cd27c96629cd1851f3356ece0bca6aa77b8393f7a0dfd90.png)\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=-1) & ≈P(-1-0.5\\le Y\\le -1+0.5) \\\\  & =P(-1.5\\le Y\\le -0.5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-1.5$ and $b=-0.5.$",
